{
  "name": "WF-01 - Alarm Ingestion Webhook",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WF-01: Alarm Ingestion Webhook\n\nEntry point for ALL fiber alarms (any vendor/system).\n\n1. Receives raw alarm via HTTPS POST\n2. Validates required fields\n3. Wraps payload into the Standard Alarm Envelope\n4. Hands off (Milestone 3) to WF-02 Normalizer\n\nSecured with Header Auth token. See README.md for setup.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 320
      },
      "id": "d1dc5ef0-8915-4088-ba6d-8d9c43a819af",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "fiber-alarm-ingest",
        "options": {
          "responseData": "{\"status\": \"received\", \"message\": \"Alarm accepted for processing\"}"
        }
      },
      "id": "b353ee6d-59b9-405f-96e0-bbf11787934c",
      "name": "1. Alarm Ingestion Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        32,
        272
      ],
      "webhookId": "REPLACE_WITH_GENERATED_WEBHOOK_ID"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// 2. Extract & Validate Payload\n// - Reads the raw alarm body\n// - Checks required fields are present. Vendor-agnostic on purpose: only\n//   'source' is required here. No real vendor NMS/EMS sends fields named\n//   'siteId'/'alarmType' (those are WF-02's *normalized output* field\n//   names) -- per-vendor raw field validation is WF-02's job, not WF-01's.\n//   See PRODUCTION_VALIDATION_REPORT.md Finding 1.\n// - Generates a correlationId (UUID) and receivedAt timestamp\n\nfunction generateUUID() {\n  return 'xxxxxxxx-xxxx-4xxx-yxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx'.replace(/[xy]/g, function (c) {\n    const r = (Math.random() * 16) | 0;\n    const v = c === 'x' ? r : (r & 0x3) | 0x8;\n    return v.toString(16);\n  });\n}\n\nconst requiredFields = ['source'];\nconst items = $input.all();\nconst results = [];\n\nfor (const item of items) {\n  const body = item.json.body ? item.json.body : item.json;\n\n  const missing = requiredFields.filter(\n    (f) => body[f] === undefined || body[f] === null || body[f] === ''\n  );\n\n  results.push({\n    json: {\n      isValid: missing.length === 0,\n      missingFields: missing,\n      correlationId: generateUUID(),\n      receivedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n      rawPayload: body\n    }\n  });\n}\n\nreturn results;"
      },
      "id": "b23d46ec-c827-4bca-b236-db18765fa404",
      "name": "2. Extract & Validate Payload",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        240,
        272
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 1
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "cond-isvalid",
              "leftValue": "={{$json.isValid}}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "f235f4a7-5a8a-4396-9caf-05aaf2273d32",
      "name": "3. Is Payload Valid?",
